WEBVTT

00:00:00.019 --> 00:00:06.497
When I say job-ready Pandas, I do not mean that you need to memorize every function in the

00:00:06.497 --> 00:00:12.667
Pandas library. Pandas is a large library, and even experienced analysts look at the documentation regularly.

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:19.542
What matters is being comfortable with the core patterns that appear repeatedly.

00:00:19.542 --> 00:00:25.267
You should know how to load data and inspect the rows, columns, data types, missing values, and duplicates.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:32.967
You should be able to select the columns you need, filter rows using business conditions,

00:00:32.967 --> 00:00:33.472
and sort or rank records.

00:00:33.472 --> 00:00:40.767
You should also be comfortable cleaning values, converting data types, standardizing text, working with dates,

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:44.112
creating new columns, and summarizing groups.

00:00:44.112 --> 00:00:47.762
Another important skill is combining tables correctly.

00:00:47.762 --> 00:00:55.222
A merge that looks successful can still be wrong if the relationship between the keys is not what

00:00:55.222 --> 00:00:58.457
you expected. Finally, you should validate your work.

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:05.627
Check row counts, totals, unique keys, and missing values after major transformations.

00:01:05.627 --> 00:01:08.647
The goal is not just to make the code run.

00:01:08.647 --> 00:01:13.523
The goal is to produce an analytical result that you can explain and defend.
